# WazHack/ZX CONCEPT round-3 wall tiles — DRAFT (replaces the round-2 solid-plaster idea).
# Format = tools/gfx_convert.py --mode tile. User direction: walls read as BLACK, with
# occasional patches of light DITHERED brick. Bricks are in register with the existing WALL
# tile (mortar rows 0/4, verticals x 0/4 then 2/6): faces = 50% checker ink, mortar = paper.
# wall_dark       : black + 4 mortar-corner dots (so a wall still reads as a wall); all borders dark
# wall_dith       : dithered bricks to every border; tiles with itself
# wall_dith_patch : an irregular dithered patch, dark at the top/bottom borders and mostly dark
#                   at the sides (it may touch a neighbour patch); tiles with wall_dark
# wall_dith_fade  : sparse (25%) dither on top -> full dither below; dark above, wall_dith below
# Ink = the level scheme's wall ink (attr only); paper always black (air band, F9).
=== wall_dark ink:blue paper:black
#...#...
........
........
........
..#...#.
........
........
........

=== wall_dith ink:blue paper:black
........
.#.#.#.#
..#...#.
.#.#.#.#
........
.#.#.#.#
#...#...
.#.#.#.#

=== wall_dith_patch ink:blue paper:black
#...#...
.#.#.#..
..#...#.
.#.#.#.#
........
.#.#.#.#
....#...
........


=== wall_dith_fade ink:blue paper:black
#...#...
..#...#.
........
..#...#.
........
.#.#.#.#
#...#...
.#.#.#.#

